=== B. patch 23 first hunk (verbatim, cat -A first 30 lines) ===
From: DBY-W09 kernel-port draft$
Subject: [PATCH DRAFT] scsi: ufs: qcom: route SM8250 UFS OPP to RPMhPD$
$
For an SM8250 UFS host with the supported two-domain topology, attach MMCX$
as power-domains index 0 and keep GCC UFS_PHY_GDSC as index 1. The generic$
device-core GenPD attach path intentionally skips consumers with multiple$
power-domains, so the Qualcomm UFS probe owns the attach-list operation.$
$
Before attaching the domains, validate every available UFS OPP entry:$
each entry must have exactly one required-opps reference to the SM8250$
RPMhPD provider's exact operating-points-v2 table. Then map required_dev$
slot 0 to the MMCX virtual GenPD device before ufshcd_pltfrm_init() adds$
the UFS OPP table.$
$
The one-domain generic path is unchanged. Unsupported multi-domain$
arrangements fail closed because the generic GenPD core skips them rather$
than attaching any one of their domains. This defines the currently$
supported two-domain contract for SM8250 UFS hosts; DBY-W09 is the board$
currently adding this topology.$
$
The code uses PD_FLAG_DEV_LINK_ON so the attached suppliers are$
runtime-active while the UFS consumer is active. It deliberately does not$
use PD_FLAG_REQUIRED_OPP, because this OPP table has one required-OPP slot,$
not one slot for each attached domain.$
$
This patch does not implement MMCX-to-MX parent propagation. ROUND30 records$
that this remains a separate unresolved HOS4.3 corner-equivalence gate.$
$
Draft only: not applied to a full kernel tree, compiled, checkpatched,$
schema-validated or tested on hardware.$

